
## Module Dependencies

### Layered Dependency Rules
1. Domain layer can only depend on standard library modules
2. Application layer depends on domain and infrastructure interfaces
3. Infrastructure layer depends on all other layers' interfaces
4. Presentation layer depends on application services

### Circular Dependency Prevention
- Never import from a module that imports from the current module
- Use dependency injection to break circular dependencies
- Consider refactoring into separate modules when necessary

## Testing Guidelines

Each module should have:
1. Unit tests for all public methods
2. Integration tests for complex interactions
3. Mock implementations of interfaces where needed
4. Test coverage reporting configuration

## Documentation Requirements

Every module must include:
1. Module-level docstring with description and purpose
2. Class docstrings for each class (public APIs)
3. Function docstrings for public functions/methods
4. Examples in docstrings when appropriate
5. Version information if applicable

This ensures consistency across all modules and maintains clear documentation standards.
